  "interfaceVersion": 32,
  "interfaceBaseline": "V32 keeps the established Aluvision interface while making animation browsing easier to understand and gentler to use. Customers first see clearly labelled effect groups; opening one enters a focused page with only that group’s variations, and choosing a variation is the action that starts it. A single back button returns to the originating list and moves beside the sticky LED overview only when its inline position is obscured. The active-animation action also moves one DOM button between the page and preview dock, so no duplicate or half-hidden copy remains. The spatial tunnel/wall overview appears on opening a spatial group and stays visible in its active settings. Page transitions use a light spring, smaller controls respond smoothly, and reduced-motion preferences are respected. Fixed-colour, animation-family and active-animation workspaces now share one calmer mobile hierarchy: the gallery has one instruction heading, the running animation is named before its controls, two animation colours align together with a deliberate full-width add action, and the active editor uses one frosted surface instead of nested cards. The fixed-colour wheel stays fully above the bottom navigation on first load. The same shared colour picker is reused for fixed colour and animation palettes; fine RGBW values remain exact. Search text stays at the iPhone no-zoom size. Browsing preserves selected lights and active effects. Browser verification does not prove physical receiver acceptance.",
